destroy extremely valuable items such as a ring of teleport control or 
one of free action or a wand of death.  So there should either be a way 
to have Mjollnir return into your hand at 100 percent probability 
without striking you or else to avoid any of your stuff being destroyed 
by it returning (for example, if you are shock resistant; I believe, 
currently this does not protect your equipment; other ways of destroying 
it - electric eels come to mind, might continue to exist; but Mjollnir 
should be sufficiently respectful of his mistress once she can throw it 
that it does not destroy items once it cannot give her an electric shock 
anymore; maybe it should be made intelligent for that purpose - a 
returning Mjollnir *behaves* intelligently in a way, it's not as if it 
were forced by the laws of aerodynamics such as a boomerang; then you 
could also allow other classes to throw it based on their strength but 
with the usual chance of being "blasted" on each return, where the blast 
would be accompanied by an electric shock and possible destruction of 
items).
